  "claim_status": "source_derived_unreviewed",
  "reported_status": "Source-derived arguments and inspected producer replay; new extensions separately identified as integration-derived. Source and internally derived claims remain unreviewed. External correctness, historical priority and physical validity are UNKNOWN. Exact/floating diagnostics, producer-code replay and same-team analytic criticism do not independently validate universal mathematics, novelty or scientific capability.",
  "scientific_scope_status": "Spatially homogeneous unit-rate isotropic-cutoff Maxwell equation in3D with supplied centered Gaussian scale-mixture initial sampler on known[a,b]. Exact rejection theorem requires b<3a/2 and ideal real/random access; broader full-law approximation has explicit TV error. New iid-output transient testing and measured-energy late-time approximation have distinct acquisition/output contracts. No spatial/reactive/path simulation, finite-bit certification or practical solver dominance.",
